    brand: "Titan Fitness",
    category: "Dedicated 35-degree plate-loaded hack squat",
    badge: "Best Dedicated Hack Squat",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BLR2B95J?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31jCWzWCtqL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $975",
    priceBounds: {"low":975,"high":975},
    specs: "Maker figures: 35° carriage · 700 lb capacity · linear bearings · 46.75 x 60.5 in. footprint · 190 lb",
    pros: [
      "A dedicated hack squat for under $1,000",
      "Linear bearings on steel guide rods, per Titan",
      "Flip-up racking handles you work without leaving the machine",
      "Compact and light for a plate-loaded sled, by Titan’s figures",
    ],
    cons: [
      "Little independent coverage; figures are Titan’s",
      "No leg press mode",
      "Warranty terms need checking on Titan’s site",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The hack squat to buy if you want the squat, not the leg press, and want the shortest, lightest sled on this page.",
    description: "Titan's dedicated hack squat runs a plate-loaded carriage on linear bearings and steel guide rods at 35 degrees, with flip-in and flip-out racking handles, an adjustable backrest, high-density padding, dual 9.75-inch Olympic weight sleeves and a large diamond-plated footplate that also suits standing calf raises. Titan listed it at $974.99 on 19 October; an earlier Titan listing gave $939.99. We found no hands-on review, so the figures are Titan's: a 700 lb carriage capacity, a 46.75 by 60.5 inch footprint, 45.5 inches tall, a 25.25 by 23.25 inch footplate, a 20 by 11.5 inch back pad and a 190 lb bolt-together frame. An older Titan listing for the same machine gives the same 35-degree angle and 700 lb rating. Titan positions it as the single-station alternative to its combo, which has the higher 1,000 lb capacity. Titan's product page carries only a general disclaimer, so check its warranty terms. We could not confirm an Amazon listing for this model; Titan sells it direct.",
  },
  {
    id: "powertec-leg-press-hack-squat",
    name: "Powertec Leg Press Hack Squat Combo",
    brand: "Powertec",
    category: "45-degree-style plate-loaded hack squat and leg press combo",
    badge: "Full-Size Combo",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0G7KHQY3C?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41JxrUCR6NL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$1,583–$1,979",
    priceBounds: {"low":1583,"high":1979},
    specs: "2-in-1 leg press and hack squat · 1,000 lb capacity · about 89 x 41 x 55 in. · about 375 lb (retailer figures) · model P-LPHS26",
    pros: [
      "Switches between leg press and hack squat on one sled, like the Force USA Compact",
      "A 1,000 lb capacity, given by Powertec and retailers alike",
      "From Powertec, a long-established home-gym maker, and sold on Amazon",
    ],
    cons: [
      "At about 89 inches long it is a full-size combo, not a compact one",
      "Its dimensions and weight come from retailer listings; we found no independent review",
      "Powertec does not publish a sled angle, shoulder-pad spread or height range that we could find",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The leg press and hack squat combo to buy on Amazon for less than the Body-Solid, if you have the room for a full-size frame and will confirm its figures with the seller.",
    description: "Titan's Leg Press Hack Squat combo, which the guide below uses as its worked example because a hands-on review documents it, is sold on Titan's own store rather than on Amazon US, so this card shows the combo Amazon does sell from an established maker: Powertec's Leg Press Hack Squat Combo. Powertec's page and retailer listings describe a plate-loaded machine that switches between leg press and hack squat modes on one sled, rated for 1,000 lb, and retailers give the model as P-LPHS26, a footprint of about 89 by 41 by 55 inches and a product weight of about 375 lb. Those dimensions come from retailer listings and we found no independent review, so treat them as the seller's figures and confirm them before ordering, along with the shoulder-pad spacing if you are tall or broad. At about 89 inches long it needs about the same floor as the other combos here. Powertec's page showed a $1,979 list price and a lower $1,682.15 price with stock marked as restocking; Amazon listed it at $1,583.20 on 9 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "bells-of-steel-leg-press-hack-squat",
    name: "Bells of Steel Leg Press Hack Squat Machine",
    brand: "Bells of Steel",
    category: "Plate-loaded leg press, hack squat and calf raise on linear bearings",
    badge: "Best Warranty",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0CQ2YNHCN?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31GpZnsSwWL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "About $2,054",
    priceBounds: {"low":2054,"high":2054},
